# The helper pid is now ComputerSessionPool::helper_pid (the helper's own process id, read from the spawn); `DevComputerHost` is
# implemented by ComputerSessionPool in dev_computer.rs, so the pool is passed twice (as the sessions and as the host). No other
# compose, Cargo or SERVICE_PENDING change: the daemon already depends on mixdog-core, mixdog-core-session, mixdog-tools.
# dev/computer/run now also answers the helper's raw commands (click, type, key, list_windows, sequence, set_value, close_window,
# focus_window, ...), the lifecycle controls (session_release, session_abort, execution_end) and read_authorization,
# update_authorization (field `authorization`), authorization_windows. No protocol row changes: `command` stays an untyped object.

file: callers of computer_pixels (s3-18, the capture of a screen and of a zoom)
# capture_display(desktop, blobs, frames, ocr, command, cancel) and zoom_display(desktop, blobs, frames, ocr, command, cancel) take
# `ocr: Option<&dyn computer_pixels::DisplayOcr>`: the recognizer is the helper's `ocr_image` over the pool (request
# {action: "ocr_image", image_base64, ocr_language, max_ocr_words, read_only: true}; its result is what the trait answers). With None an
# automatic recognition is not made and an asked one (include_ocr) says the helper returned no OCR.
# `capture_display` now answers the screen capture's reply fields (coordinate_space, pixel_status, accessibility_status, total_elements,
# returned_elements, total_accessibility_elements, elements, ocr_elements), so it replaces `capture_screen`'s reply as it is.
# The desktop's host/computer/pixels handler (s3-22) crops to `region` (HostComputerPixelsParams.region, see the rows fragment).
